ATORY \"MADE FOR KIDS\" DESIGNATION REQUIRED)              |\n421: +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n422: ```\n423: \n424: #### Financial & Operational Penalties:\n425: - **Statutory Fines**: Maximum civil penalties of **$53,088 per violation** (FTC 16 C.F.R. § 1.98).\n426: - **The \"Made for Kids\" (MFK) Penalty**: Correctly marking content as MFK strips behavioral ads, resulting in a **60% to 90% RPM collapse** ($0.50–$1.00 RPM), disabling comments, end screens, community tabs, and notification bells.\n427: \n428: ---\n429: \n430: ### Risk 3: Repetitious & Reused Content Policy Enforcement\n431: \n432: Enforced under YouTube Channel Monetization Policies:\n433: - **Reused Content**: Content that fails to provide significant original commentary, educational value, or unique editorial transformation.\n434: - **Inauthentic / Repetitious Content**: Mass-produced, templated uploads where gameplay loops are repeated with only cosmetic asset swaps.\n435: - **The Appeal Trap**: Video appeals require showing the creator's face, screen recording of editing software (Premiere/DaVinci), and explanation of human editorial input. Rejections result in a 90-day demonetization freeze.\n436: \n437: ---\n438: \n439: ### Risk 4: Copyright Strike Risk from Marvel, Sony, and Disney\n440: \n441: #### Intellectual Property Architecture & Fair Use Failure\n442: \n443: ```\n444:                       +------------------------------------------------+\n445:                       |      SONY / INSOMNIAC PC BINARIES (ENCRYPTED)  |\n446:                       +-----------------------+------------------------+\n447:                                               | (Unauthorized Asset Rip via NinjaRipper)\n448:                                               v\n449:                       +------------------------------------------------+\n450:                       |     EXTRACTED .OBJ / .YDD 3D CHARACTER MESH    |\n451:          